{
  "Navigates through pages of items, with page size options, the current position, navigation buttons and a button for each nearby page. It switches to a compact layout when it does not fit, and it looks and works like the DataGrid pager.": "",
  "`x-model` binds the page, and `onPageChanged` also reports the page size, so data can be loaded for both.": "",
  "A `nav` named “Pages” in the kit language, or by its label.": "",
  "Each page button is named “Page 5”, and the current one has `aria-current=\"page\"`.": "",
  "Named First page, Previous page, Next page and Last page, and disabled at the ends.": "",
  "The page number box is named “Page number”, and the information stays available to screen readers while hidden.": "",
  "The pagination. `data-look`: `full` or `compact`.": "Pagination. `data-look`: `full` ya da `compact`.",
  "The page sizes, as buttons or a drop-down.": "",
  "The information text, a navigation button (`data-step`), the page buttons and the gaps.": "",
  "The page number box in the compact layout.": "",
  "The appearance of its buttons, which matches the DataGrid pager in each design language.": "",
  "Unit: the information text.": "",
  "The spacing between parts, the double arrows and the boxes in the compact layout.": "",
  "The page number, starting from 1.": "",
  "Same as `page`. This is what `x-model` binds, with two-way binding.": "",
  "The total number of items. The page count is derived from this and `pageSize`.": "",
  "The number of items per page. 0 shows all items on one page.": "",
  "The number of pages, when there is no `total`.": "",
  "The available page sizes (0 means all). Changing the size keeps the first item of the page in view.": "",
  "“Page 3 of 12 (250 items)”.": "“Sayfa 3 / 12 (250 öğe)”.",
  "The first, previous, next and last buttons.": "",
  "The number of page buttons on each side of the current page.": "",
  "`full`, `compact` (a page number box and a drop-down of sizes), or `adaptive`, which is compact when the full layout does not fit.": "",
  "Custom information text. `{page}`, `{count}` and `{total}` are replaced with their values.": "",
  "The accessible name. If a page has several, each one needs its own.": "",
  "Occurs when the page or the page size changes (`page`, `pageSize`), either by the user or programmatically (`byUser`).": "",
  "Goes to a page, starting from 1, as a click would.": "",
  "Read-only": "",
  "The current number of pages.": "",
  "Indicates whether the compact layout is currently shown.": ""
